=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 419
title: a Makefile that builds stays production, but its edit no longer holds a weakened Python assertion at warn
origin: successor of build_makefile_stays_prod_neg with the same inputs, re-pinned by the #419 ruling
origin2: (issuecomment-6170353038: Q1 (b), Q5 (b), rule 2). The discriminator is unchanged: a C build
origin3: recipe is production, not ci, and the exact finding count still forbids CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED.
origin4: What moved is the credit: a Python test refuses opaque-change evidence for ASSERT_WEAKENED.
=== before: Makefile ===
CFLAGS = -O1

_speedups.so: _speedups.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -shared -o $@ $<
=== after: Makefile ===
CFLAGS = -O2

_speedups.so: _speedups.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -shared -o $@ $<
=== before: tests/test_speed.py ===
from app import fast_add


def test_fast_add():
    assert fast_add(3, 4) == 7
=== after: tests/test_speed.py ===
from app import fast_add


def test_fast_add():
    assert fast_add(3, 4) > 0
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "ASSERT_WEAKENED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["OPAQUE_PROD_CHANGE_NOT_EVIDENCE"]}]
